│ Analyzing collected context:                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  1 What does this part of the code do?                             │
│                                                                    │
│ In src/agentscope/model/_dashscope_model.py, the code snippets     │
│ show two places where _json_loads_with_repair is called to parse   │
│ the "arguments" of tool calls during response parsing. The first   │
│ snippet processes accumulated tool calls in a loop and converts    │
│ their argument strings into dictionaries, adding them as           │
│ ToolUseBlock content blocks. The second snippet processes a        │
│ message's tool_calls in a similar fashion, converting argument     │
│ JSON strings into dictionaries before adding ToolUseBlock          │
│ instances to the content blocks.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ In src/agentscope/model/_openai_model.py, within the               │
│ OpenAIChatModel class's _parse_openai_completion_response method,  │
│ the code iterates over tool_calls in the response's choice         │
│ message. For each tool_call, it uses _json_loads_with_repair on    │
│ the function.arguments to parse the JSON string into a dictionary  │
│ before creating a ToolUseBlock.                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│ These locations are exactly where the issue is introduced: the     │
│ calls to _json_loads_with_repair are made eagerly during           │
│ streaming/response parsing without checking if the content is      │
│ complete. The bug report explains that when parsing complex        │
│ multi-line JSON or YAML strings prematurely (i.e., partial or      │
│ incomplete data), the _json_loads_with_repair function may cause   │
│ hangs or crashes. Because these parts of the code call the         │
│ function unconditionally on intermediate streaming outputs (e.g.,  │
│ tool-call argument strings), they exhibit the buggy behavior       │
│ described.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│ The intended behavior is to avoid calling _json_loads_with_repair  │
│ on incomplete tool-call argument data during streaming. Instead,   │
│ the system should buffer or treat these arguments as raw text      │
│ until it detects the stream is complete (e.g., when last=True or   │
│ equivalent). Only after receiving full, complete data should       │
│ _json_loads_with_repair be applied. This reduces parsing errors    │
│ and prevents the crashes or hangs seen on partial inputs. The      │
│ existing functionality of parsing tool-call arguments into         │
│ dictionaries and converting them into ToolUseBlocks should be      │
│ preserved, with the addition of guarding the call with a           │
│ content-completeness check or buffering mechanism.                 │
│                                                                    │
│ Conclusion:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix involves modifying the methods in _dashscope_model.py and  │
│ _openai_model.py that currently call _json_loads_with_repair on    │
│ tool-call arguments to ensure they only do so after the full       │
│ content is received. Until then, tool-call parameters should be    │
│ treated as raw text. This will stabilize the agent system under    │
│ complex streaming output scenarios.                                │
