│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • The bug relates to calling _json_loads_with_repair prematurely  │
│    on incomplete streaming outputs, especially for multiline JSON  │
│    or YAML content.                                                │
│  • In the async generator method, argument strings are built by    │
│    concatenating chunks, but no indication is managed to parse     │
│    only after stream completion.                                   │
│  • The synchronous method immediately parses tool call arguments   │
│    assuming full data availability.                                │
│  • This leads to potential crashes or hangs when                   │
│    _json_loads_with_repair operates on fragmented or partial       │
│    JSON/YAML.                                                      │
│  • There is no guard or check to defer parsing to only after the   │
│    final chunk or full content is received.                        │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • The asynchronous method accumulating argument chunks should     │
│    buffer incoming partial argument strings per tool call until    │
│    detecting the final chunk (e.g., last=True or stream end).      │
│  • It should call _json_loads_with_repair only once on the         │
│    complete argument string, not on intermediate fragments.        │
│  • The synchronous method parsing the message's tool calls should  │
│    only do so after full content receipt, typically safe as        │
│    parsing complete responses.                                     │
│  • For streaming scenarios, parsing should be deferred similarly.  │
│  • Overall, the system should treat streamed tool call arguments   │
│    as raw text until stream completion, then parse robustly.       │
│  • This change will prevent hangs or crashes from premature        │
│    parsing while preserving existing parsing and response          │
│    construction.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Conclusion:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • The fix requires modifying the async response parsing method to │
│    detect completeness before parsing arguments.                   │
│  • It also requires cautious parsing in other response methods to  │
│    ensure arguments are fully received.                            │
│  • This aligns with the issue's expected behavior that             │
│    _json_loads_with_repair should only be triggered on complete    │
│    data.                                                           │
